==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɛld/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-geld.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛld|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰeldʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|geld}} (and reinforced by {{cog|la-med|geldum}}), both from {{inh|en|ang|ġeld}}, {{m|ang|ġield|t=payment, tribute}} (which regularly yield {{m|en|yield}}), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*geld}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*geldą|t=reward, gift, money}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰeldʰ-|t=to pay}}. Probably reinforced by {{m|en|gelt}} (which see), see {{cog|nb|gjeld|t=debt}}, {{cog|da|gæld|t=debt}} (whence apparently the otherwise irregular hard ''g'' in Middle English ''geld'' and perhaps also in Medieval Latin ''geldum'', as opposed to the regular continuation ''yield'' from Old English). {{m|en||Geld}} is also written {{m|en|gelt}} or {{m|en|gild}}, and as such found in {{m|en|wergild}}, {{m|en|Danegeld}}, ''etc.'' {{dbt|en|yield}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|jild|t=money}}, {{cog|stq|Jield}}, {{m|stq|Jäild|t=money}}, {{cog|nl|geld|t=money}}, {{cog|de|Geld|t=money}}, {{cog|non|gjald|t=payment}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌹𐌻𐌳|t=tribute}}. Also related to {{cog|en|yield}}.
{{col-bottom}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|archaic|dialectal|or|historical}} [[money|Money]].
## {{lb|en|Northern England}} A [[payment]].
## {{lb|en|historical}} In particular, (money paid as) a [[medieval]] form of land [[tax]].

